  "notes": "Official cause_code/category is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields (block 13 empty), so cause node marked provisional per rule 4, despite narrative describing a clear latent procedural/human-performance error. SSF is modeled as a non-EIIS System per plant design description; ASW here refers to SSF Auxiliary Service Water, a distinct SSF subsystem declared inoperable due to heater status, not the plant's main ASW system. No backup systems were stated as operable during the inoperability window itself (SSF ASW/RC Makeup/PSW are discussed only in hypothetical safety-analysis context for a postulated future SSF-activation event, not as operable backups during this actual inoperability period) — so no BACKED_UP_BY edges emitted per rule 6. No previous similar occurrence LER was identified (explicitly stated none found), so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge emitted."
